  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\) and \\(\\triangle DBC\\), \\(BC=BC\\) (common side), \\(\\angle ABC=\\angle DBC\\), and \\(\\angle ACB=\\angle DCB\\). Which criterion is used to prove that the two triangles are congruent?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "SSS",
    "B": "SAS",
    "C": "ASA",
    "D": "HL"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(BC\\) is the included side between \\(\\angle ABC\\) and \\(\\angle ACB\\). Two angles and their included side are respectively equal, so use ASA.",
